---
title: Mammals
description: Measurement fields for specimens in a Mammalogy catalog.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

Specimens in a project that uses the `Mammalogy` catalog format show the mammal
measurement form. Sex, life stage, and weight units work the same way in every
taxon group; see [Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/).

## Measurements

- `Total length (mm)`: the total length from the tip of the nose to the tip of
  the tail.
- `Tail length (mm)`: the length of the tail from the base to the tip.
- `Head and body length (mm)`: auto-calculated from `Total length (mm) - Tail length (mm)`.
- `Tail/HB length`: auto-calculated from `Tail length (mm) / Head and body length (mm)`.
- `Hind foot length (mm)`: the length of the hind foot from the base to the tip of the claw.
- `Ear length (mm)`: ear length.
- `Weight`: specimen weight in the selected unit.
- `Accuracy`: `Accurate` or `Inaccurate`. Choosing `Inaccurate` opens
  `Select inaccurate measurements`, where you tick each affected measurement
  (total, tail, hind foot, ear, and weight, plus forearm and tibia when bat
  fields are shown), and an `Accuracy remark` field for the reason. Exports and
  labels can bracket the flagged values.
- `Sex`: select from the configured specimen-sex vocabulary.
- `Life stage`: select from the configured life-stage vocabulary.
- `Remarks`: additional notes about measurements.

Turn on `Show outlier warnings` to flag measurements that look unusual for the
taxon. Changing `Sex` asks `Change sex?` and clears reproductive data that no
longer applies.

## Reproductive data

| Sex | Field | Options |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Male | Testis `Position` | Scrotal, Abdominal |
| Male | Testis length and width (mm) | Numbers |
| Male | Epididymis appearance | Tubular, Partial, Not Tubular |
| Female | Vagina opening | Imperforate, Perforate |
| Female | Pubic symphysis | Close, Small Open, Open |
| Female | Reproductive stage | Nulliparous, Primiparous, Multiparous |
| Female | Mammae condition | Small, Large, Lactating |
| Female | Mammae counts | Axillary, abdominal, and inguinal pairs |
| Female | Placental scars, embryos | Counted left and right |
| Female | Embryo `CR length (mm)` | Crown-rump length |

## Bat fields

Turn on `Show bat fields` on a specimen to add forearm length, tibia length,
`Echolocate?`, echolocation type (`FM`, `CF`, `QCF`, or `None`), maximum and
minimum frequency, frequency at maximum energy, and duration. To show them on
every mammal specimen, turn on `Always show bat fields` in `Settings` >
`Catalogs` > `Format`. A specimen with saved bat data always shows the section.

## Parts and symbionts

Mammal catalogs show symbiont-detection fields and the symbiont tab. See
[Specimen Parts](/en/usages/specimens/parts/).
